{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to `d77d780c`: the second LS-5 diagnostic ran on Linux.\n\nHead `86221eb3372aa9df999f225e2b30ecb823968959`, branch\n`diag/ls5b-20261115`, Local Worker smoke run 43789667876, failure.\nThe closed line, complete:\n\n- `stage: smoke`, `signal: null`, `operation: install`,\n  `detail: transport-no-answer`.\n- `transport`: `kind: reply-not-answer`, `status: 4xx`,\n  `statusCode: 410`.\n- `exchange`: `clientPhase: response-complete`,\n  `firstFailure: none`, `errorClass: none`,\n  `proxyDecision: forwarded`, `upstreamPhase: response-complete`,\n  `upstreamEnd: complete`, `downstreamEnd: finished`,\n  `clientBodyEnd: complete`, `clientStop: none`,\n  `upstreamStatus: 4xx`, `clientStatus: 4xx`,\n  `startupHealth: http-503`, `startupSessions: ok`,\n  `proxy: listening`, `worker: running`,\n  `upstreamStatusCode: 410`, `clientStatusCode: 410`,\n  `replyBodyClass: json-worker-room-retired-shape`,\n  `faultBoundary: backend-reply`, `owner: celldbackend`.\n- `roomFormat`, one record: `method: observed-create`,\n  `result: retired-stop`, `observer: installed`,\n  `restoration: restored`.\n  `catalog`: `state: returned`, `rows: one`, `shape: exact`,\n  `cells: [number-one, number-zero]`.\n  `word`: `state: not-called`, `rows: unknown`, `shape: unknown`,\n  `cells: [missing]`.\n\nSo the new object's storage holds a table before the classifier\nreads it, and it holds no `room_record_format` table. The classifier\nthen judges a new room as retired. Under celld every new room gets\n410. That breaks self-hosting, and the smoke is right to fail.\n\nNext, under LS-5:\n\n1. Name the table that the storage holds at that read, from the\n   celld or workerd source or from one more closed diagnostic. A\n   diagnostic prints a closed class of the name, and no name that a\n   member wrote.\n2. Propose the fix before source. My preference, for you to test\n   against the source: the classifier recognizes a retired room by\n   the tables that the earlier room format wrote, and a table of the\n   host does not count. Say whether a retired room can then be\n   mistaken for a new one, and show the case that proves it cannot.\n3. Say whether the fix changes a Worker bundle only, and where it\n   lands in the order.\n\nDecision on `3aef7ffe`, the CR-2 Native witness: accepted. The case\nsupplies the labelled presence-only `ARTIFACTS: {}` object, as\n`creation-admission.test.ts:118` does, and keeps the stated\n`OutsideDouble`. Each install, found, child and enrollment judgment\nstays real. The witness on the live Worker is mine, after the\nlanding.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}